# Load a frozen fixture standing on the bottom level of the dungeon,
# levitating over a chasm, and ask to descend. (bd inc-30ps)
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/levitate-bottom-seed1.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/levitate-bottom-load.keys 1
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. tools/keys/levitate-bottom.keys walks nine wizard depth
# jumps to GENERATE this situation, and generation consumes the shared random
# stream -- an unrelated change to src/ that makes different rolls on the way
# down can hand back a depth 10 with no chasm at all, which happened to this
# check under inc-30ps (the combat rework moved the rolls). This script
# builds no character and generates no map: it LOADS the frozen fixture
# tools/keys/levitate-bottom-save.keys already stood on a chasm, levitating,
# so the situation survives a change that moves unrelated rolls. See
# tools/fixtures/README.md and bd inc-1fjk.
#
# The Goblin Caves declares DUN_DEPTH 10 (lib/dungeon.irh), so depth 10 is the
# bottom and Creature::Descend's levitation branch asks GetDungeonMap for
# depth 11 -- one past the last handle the allocation holds.

@dump:on-bottom

# Ask to go down while levitating over the chasm.
>
@dump:after-descend

# Decline whatever prompt the request raised, so the session ends where it
# started and the depth reading is readable on the last screen.
n
@dump:settled
@quit
